1
00:00:48,850 --> 00:00:52,890
[The Old Story of Yu Hong]

2
00:00:53,240 --> 00:00:55,920
[Episode 19]

3
00:00:56,850 --> 00:00:57,500
Name?

4
00:00:58,350 --> 00:00:59,030
Zhang Zhiqiang.

5
00:00:59,520 --> 00:01:00,140
Age?

6
00:01:00,740 --> 00:01:01,250
Forty.

7
00:01:01,520 --> 00:01:01,970
What?

8
00:01:02,390 --> 00:01:02,930
Forty.

9
00:01:03,060 --> 00:01:03,750
Captain.

10
00:01:03,750 --> 00:01:05,180
Is this what you wanted to see?

11
00:01:07,350 --> 00:01:08,450
Wang, keep questioning him.

12
00:01:14,920 --> 00:01:15,590
He Liang.

13
00:01:16,650 --> 00:01:17,600
Take a look at these two.

14
00:01:18,710 --> 00:01:19,640
Are these what you're looking for?

15
00:01:27,760 --> 00:01:29,510
Fake. All made of dog skin.

16
00:01:32,410 --> 00:01:34,590
[Public Security]

17
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:34,560
I heard you helped

18
00:01:35,090 --> 00:01:36,789
our criminal investigation
team score big today.

19
00:01:38,370 --> 00:01:39,780
It's not the same thing
as what I'm investigating.

20
00:01:39,810 --> 00:01:41,670
Still can't find any lead related

21
00:01:41,759 --> 00:01:42,550
to Zhao Changyou.

22
00:01:42,729 --> 00:01:43,479
Alright.

23
00:01:44,020 --> 00:01:45,430
Something's better than nothing.

24
00:01:46,560 --> 00:01:47,729
Is that portrait...

25
00:01:48,210 --> 00:01:48,900
at the station?

26
00:01:49,509 --> 00:01:50,200
It's with me.

27
00:01:50,590 --> 00:01:51,140
What's wrong?

28
00:01:51,140 --> 00:01:51,870
Let me borrow it.

29
00:01:52,020 --> 00:01:53,160
I'll study it more.

30
00:01:54,350 --> 00:01:55,140
You're back.

31
00:01:56,930 --> 00:01:57,700
Have you eaten?

32
00:02:04,630 --> 00:02:06,310
He hasn't given me a good look all day.

33
00:02:08,470 --> 00:02:10,900
This new job is like being an escort.

34
00:02:11,620 --> 00:02:12,650
Never at home.

35
00:02:14,460 --> 00:02:15,570
He smells like booze.

36
00:02:15,590 --> 00:02:16,740
Must've eaten already.

37
00:02:17,510 --> 00:02:18,410
The other day,

38
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:20,560
I saw him on the street
in Chen Hong's car.

39
00:02:20,579 --> 00:02:21,710
Scared the hell out of me.

40
00:02:21,740 --> 00:02:23,120
I thought it was Wang Liye.

41
00:02:23,930 --> 00:02:25,660
You know, this new job of my brother's—

42
00:02:25,690 --> 00:02:27,120
he's filling a suspect's old spot.

43
00:02:27,140 --> 00:02:29,190
No matter how I think about it,
it gives me the creeps.

44
00:02:30,220 --> 00:02:31,350
A job like his—

45
00:02:31,380 --> 00:02:32,550
most people wouldn't dare take it.

46
00:02:33,430 --> 00:02:34,250
So what are we supposed to do?

47
00:02:34,250 --> 00:02:35,560
Jobs are hard to find these days.

48
00:02:35,750 --> 00:02:36,560
Working for a female boss

49
00:02:36,560 --> 00:02:37,840
is better than a male one, right?

50
00:02:37,940 --> 00:02:39,220
At least women don't
drink, gamble, or visit prostitutes.

51
00:02:40,320 --> 00:02:41,780
As long as Yang stays on the right path

52
00:02:41,780 --> 00:02:42,620
and doesn't go bad,

53
00:02:42,620 --> 00:02:44,079
I can put my mind at ease.

54
00:04:07,250 --> 00:04:08,690
Let me tell you a story.

55
00:04:10,040 --> 00:04:11,420
Just pretend I'm talking nonsense.

56
00:04:12,130 --> 00:04:14,680
Would an ordinary person
dare drive Chen Hong's car?

57
00:04:22,650 --> 00:04:23,560
Suppose—

58
00:04:24,170 --> 00:04:25,320
I'm just saying suppose—

59
00:04:25,840 --> 00:04:28,530
Liu Yang came back
to Tiecheng for Chen Hong.

60
00:04:28,620 --> 00:04:31,050
The two of them plotted to kill Li Dewu,

61
00:04:31,310 --> 00:04:33,130
then framed Wang Liye.

62
00:04:33,460 --> 00:04:34,720
After cutting off a hand,

63
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:37,070
they tossed it into Wang Liye's car.

64
00:04:37,070 --> 00:04:39,250
Once everything blew over,

65
00:04:39,420 --> 00:04:42,060
Liu Yang openly became

66
00:04:42,060 --> 00:04:43,800
part of Chen Hong's company.

67
00:04:46,260 --> 00:04:47,659
Later, maybe

68
00:04:47,930 --> 00:04:49,370
he even becomes a legit boss.

69
00:04:53,630 --> 00:04:55,340
Doesn't that sound pretty plausible?

70
00:05:02,140 --> 00:05:02,980
Juan.

71
00:05:04,050 --> 00:05:05,420
Just consider me talking nonsense.

72
00:05:05,930 --> 00:05:07,430
These are newly
roasted sunflower seeds from Mr. Wang's.

73
00:05:07,430 --> 00:05:08,930
I specifically asked him
to roast them a bit burnt.

74
00:05:11,680 --> 00:05:12,430
You can be mad at me,

75
00:05:12,430 --> 00:05:13,360
but don't mistreat your stomach.

76
00:05:15,430 --> 00:05:16,330
Come on, come here.

77
00:05:20,820 --> 00:05:22,120
I feed you and house you,

78
00:05:22,150 --> 00:05:23,170
treating you like a guest all day.

79
00:05:23,190 --> 00:05:23,990
And what do you do?

80
00:05:24,020 --> 00:05:25,140
You suspect my brother.

81
00:05:25,280 --> 00:05:26,460
Aren't you just an ungrateful wretch?

82
00:05:26,870 --> 00:05:28,220
Just take it as a joke.

83
00:05:28,220 --> 00:05:29,980
I also said it was just a story.

84
00:05:29,980 --> 00:05:31,360
Who jokes about a murderer?

85
00:05:31,500 --> 00:05:32,760
And you call yourself a cop?

86
00:05:33,570 --> 00:05:34,690
And let me tell you,

87
00:05:34,720 --> 00:05:36,760
my brother has a girlfriend named Hao Jie.

88
00:05:37,060 --> 00:05:38,120
She's his former classmate.

89
00:05:38,590 --> 00:05:39,730
They're really good together.

90
00:05:39,880 --> 00:05:41,230
My brother has no reason
to fool around with anyone else.

91
00:05:42,310 --> 00:05:43,250
If you dare run your mouth again,

92
00:05:43,250 --> 00:05:44,070
I'll kick you out.

93
00:05:44,070 --> 00:05:44,720
Believe it or not.

94
00:05:45,380 --> 00:05:46,190
Juan.

95
00:05:46,909 --> 00:05:47,700
Come on.

96
00:05:49,050 --> 00:05:49,570
I'm sorry.

97
00:05:49,590 --> 00:05:50,790
I apologize to you.

98
00:05:52,700 --> 00:05:53,200
Don't be mad.

99
00:05:58,300 --> 00:05:59,860
How's the new job?

100
00:06:00,720 --> 00:06:01,510
It's okay.

101
00:06:03,670 --> 00:06:05,670
Getting along with your coworkers?

102
00:06:08,150 --> 00:06:09,420
I'm just a driver.

103
00:06:09,420 --> 00:06:10,890
I'm around the boss all day.

104
00:06:10,890 --> 00:06:12,480
Don't really deal with coworkers much.

105
00:06:15,450 --> 00:06:17,100
Is your boss good to you?

106
00:06:21,750 --> 00:06:22,980
They sit while I stand.

107
00:06:22,980 --> 00:06:24,390
They eat and drink while I watch.

108
00:06:26,540 --> 00:06:27,430
It's just a job.

109
00:06:27,430 --> 00:06:28,720
Can't really say good or bad.

110
00:06:30,570 --> 00:06:31,860
Then your boss—

111
00:06:38,310 --> 00:06:39,300
Why don't you answer it?

112
00:06:41,659 --> 00:06:42,930
Maybe it's an emergency.

113
00:06:44,510 --> 00:06:45,250
It's fine.

114
00:06:45,250 --> 00:06:46,390
What emergency could there be?

115
00:06:47,010 --> 00:06:48,900
Besides, nothing's more
important than being with you.

116
00:06:49,510 --> 00:06:50,980
What, a driver's not allowed

117
00:06:50,980 --> 00:06:52,220
to date and take a walk?

118
00:06:55,300 --> 00:06:55,740
Let's go.

119
00:07:05,630 --> 00:07:07,360
What's the farthest place
you've ever been?

120
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:09,870
Farthest?

121
00:07:11,270 --> 00:07:12,630
I've been to...

122
00:07:12,630 --> 00:07:13,420
Fujian

123
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:14,890
and Guangxi.

124
00:07:15,500 --> 00:07:16,160
Places you've

125
00:07:16,160 --> 00:07:17,680
never heard of—

126
00:07:18,190 --> 00:07:19,060
Changle,

127
00:07:19,660 --> 00:07:20,690
Xianyou.

128
00:07:21,860 --> 00:07:22,540
And one called

129
00:07:22,810 --> 00:07:23,680
Qingliu.

130
00:07:24,630 --> 00:07:25,510
Xianyou?

131
00:07:26,500 --> 00:07:28,140
"Thus forming a dream of the southwest,

132
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:29,520
dreaming of being a guest in Xianyou."

133
00:07:32,670 --> 00:07:34,830
And Yunmeng in Hubei.

134
00:07:35,310 --> 00:07:36,690
Leling in Shandong.

135
00:07:37,830 --> 00:07:39,240
"Vapor steams from the Yunmeng Marsh;

136
00:07:39,740 --> 00:07:41,130
waves shake Yueyang City."

137
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:43,870
I've even been to Beijing.

138
00:07:43,870 --> 00:07:45,220
I went to Da... Dazhalan.

139
00:07:46,530 --> 00:07:47,860
It's pronounced Dashilan.

140
00:07:47,890 --> 00:07:50,280
And "Leling" is pronounced "Laoling".

141
00:07:51,130 --> 00:07:51,810
Laoling?

142
00:07:52,920 --> 00:07:54,010
Like the "Lao" in "Laoke"?

143
00:07:56,540 --> 00:07:57,310
When you recover,

144
00:07:57,310 --> 00:07:58,659
I'll take you to all these places.

145
00:08:02,060 --> 00:08:03,720
Then can you tell me again

146
00:08:03,830 --> 00:08:05,740
the station names
from Tiecheng to Shanghai?

147
00:08:07,500 --> 00:08:08,420
What's there to tell?

148
00:08:08,420 --> 00:08:09,060
You know those

149
00:08:09,060 --> 00:08:10,600
station names better than I do.

150
00:09:24,780 --> 00:09:25,320
It's fine.

151
00:09:25,630 --> 00:09:26,730
You should go.

152
00:09:26,870 --> 00:09:27,890
Maybe it's urgent.

153
00:09:34,390 --> 00:09:35,270
Then I'm really going.

154
00:09:39,910 --> 00:09:41,340
Before you see me next time,

155
00:09:41,700 --> 00:09:42,790
get your clothes changed.

156
00:09:45,460 --> 00:09:45,980
Okay.

157
00:09:47,910 --> 00:09:48,370
I'm leaving.

158
00:10:22,850 --> 00:10:23,440
Ms. Chen.

159
00:10:24,180 --> 00:10:25,430
Who does he think he is?

160
00:10:25,740 --> 00:10:27,510
A driver acting this cocky?

161
00:10:27,720 --> 00:10:29,060
Are we still doing business or not?

162
00:10:29,530 --> 00:10:30,370
Yes.

163
00:10:30,370 --> 00:10:31,390
Of course we are, Mr. Luo.

164
00:10:31,390 --> 00:10:32,310
Don't be mad.

165
00:10:32,460 --> 00:10:33,510
He's just new here.

166
00:10:33,510 --> 00:10:34,120
He doesn't know any better.

167
00:10:34,290 --> 00:10:35,610
I've never seen anyone like that.

168
00:10:35,630 --> 00:10:36,790
If it weren't for you,

169
00:10:36,960 --> 00:10:37,940
I'd have someone beat him up.

170
00:10:39,170 --> 00:10:40,480
I apologize to you.

171
00:10:40,600 --> 00:10:42,700
I'll beat him up for you, okay?

172
00:10:42,980 --> 00:10:44,030
How are you going to make it up to me?

173
00:10:45,960 --> 00:10:46,770
How will I make it up to you?

174
00:10:47,630 --> 00:10:48,240
Mr. Luo.

175
00:10:48,610 --> 00:10:51,170
You're not the only agent in Guangzhou.

176
00:10:51,170 --> 00:10:52,130
Don't you think?

177
00:10:52,270 --> 00:10:53,200
Wait, you—

178
00:10:53,200 --> 00:10:54,010
What do you mean?

179
00:10:58,420 --> 00:11:00,400
Do you have any idea
what a mess you've made for me?

180
00:11:03,030 --> 00:11:04,860
Do you know how strong
Mr. Luo's connections are?

181
00:11:05,010 --> 00:11:06,240
Who do you think you are?

182
00:11:06,390 --> 00:11:08,240
You think you're tougher than Mr. Luo?

183
00:11:08,620 --> 00:11:10,220
If we lose this order
worth hundreds of thousands,

184
00:11:10,220 --> 00:11:11,650
the whole company will go under.

185
00:11:11,650 --> 00:11:12,510
And you'll be out on your ass!

186
00:11:18,690 --> 00:11:20,140
Did I say you could leave?

187
00:11:29,540 --> 00:11:32,870
[Office] [General Manager]

188
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:33,670
Are you crazy?

189
00:11:33,820 --> 00:11:35,100
Yeah, I'm damn crazy.

190
00:11:35,150 --> 00:11:36,100
I'll do anything

191
00:11:36,100 --> 00:11:37,180
to make money!

192
00:11:37,390 --> 00:11:38,600
Today I'll teach you

193
00:11:38,720 --> 00:11:39,510
when to speak

194
00:11:39,510 --> 00:11:40,390
and when to keep

195
00:11:40,390 --> 00:11:41,770
your mouth shut as a driver!

196
00:11:41,770 --> 00:11:42,890
We're in your office!

197
00:11:42,890 --> 00:11:43,860
So what about that?

198
00:11:45,360 --> 00:11:46,210
Let me tell you something.

199
00:11:46,290 --> 00:11:47,840
I'm the driver you hired,

200
00:11:47,840 --> 00:11:49,220
not a gigolo you keep!

201
00:11:49,220 --> 00:11:50,050
Understand?

202
00:11:52,150 --> 00:11:53,960
And I'm not your sickly girlfriend either.

203
00:11:54,380 --> 00:11:55,930
I don't need your pity.

204
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:01,120
Stop pretending.

205
00:12:02,040 --> 00:12:03,640
Aren't you tired of playing the good guy?

206
00:12:24,470 --> 00:12:28,400
[General Manager]

207
00:13:06,860 --> 00:13:08,990
You like me, don't you?

208
00:13:13,830 --> 00:13:15,330
But the way I am now,

209
00:13:16,650 --> 00:13:18,130
my body won't allow it.

210
00:13:19,960 --> 00:13:20,890
I didn't mean that.

211
00:13:52,500 --> 00:13:53,870
His wings

212
00:13:54,220 --> 00:13:56,700
became like polished blades.

213
00:13:57,860 --> 00:14:00,360
The shriek of splitting air

214
00:14:01,090 --> 00:14:03,180
turned into a joyful murmur.

215
00:14:13,360 --> 00:14:14,170
Once I save enough money,

216
00:14:14,170 --> 00:14:16,100
I'll take you south for surgery.

217
00:14:17,290 --> 00:14:18,660
We'll get on the train from Tiecheng,

218
00:14:19,360 --> 00:14:20,530
then pass through Liaoyang.

219
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:23,860
Then Anshan, Haicheng,

220
00:14:25,390 --> 00:14:27,030
Xiliu, and Panjin.

221
00:14:27,860 --> 00:14:29,860
If we get hungry,
we'll stop at Goubangzi for roast chicken.

222
00:14:48,950 --> 00:14:49,970
[Tiedong District People's Hospital
Prepayment Receipt]

223
00:14:51,290 --> 00:14:51,640
[Tiedong District People's Hospital
Outpatient Payment Notice]

224
00:14:57,050 --> 00:14:58,630
[Tester: Zhang Wenjie] [Checker: Xu Bin]

225
00:14:58,690 --> 00:15:00,320
[Result Notice]

226
00:14:58,800 --> 00:14:59,870
What are you doing?

227
00:15:01,010 --> 00:15:01,740
What the hell is all this?

228
00:15:01,740 --> 00:15:02,750
Explain yourself. Now.

229
00:15:05,250 --> 00:15:06,410
Why are you going through my stuff?

230
00:15:06,410 --> 00:15:07,630
How do you have the nerve to ask me?

231
00:15:07,970 --> 00:15:08,530
Is there something

232
00:15:08,530 --> 00:15:09,690
wrong with your head?

233
00:15:09,770 --> 00:15:10,630
Those soybeans wouldn't sell,

234
00:15:10,660 --> 00:15:11,440
so you just ate them all?

235
00:15:11,650 --> 00:15:12,500
Stuffed yourself silly.

236
00:15:12,500 --> 00:15:13,270
Mouth flapping up top,

237
00:15:13,270 --> 00:15:14,120
ass farting down below.

238
00:15:14,440 --> 00:15:15,130
How do you get a girlfriend

239
00:15:15,130 --> 00:15:16,370
and end up risking your life?

240
00:15:16,500 --> 00:15:17,480
You don't even want your kidney?

241
00:15:17,480 --> 00:15:18,360
You're giving half of it to her?

242
00:15:18,380 --> 00:15:19,860
What were you thinking?

243
00:15:20,360 --> 00:15:21,510
Before Mom passed away,

244
00:15:21,900 --> 00:15:23,040
she specifically told me

245
00:15:23,820 --> 00:15:25,250
to take good care of you,

246
00:15:27,510 --> 00:15:28,290
to keep an eye on you,

247
00:15:28,290 --> 00:15:29,290
and not let you go astray.

248
00:15:29,840 --> 00:15:31,460
I thought since I'm a cop,

249
00:15:31,460 --> 00:15:32,500
you'd be right under my nose,

250
00:15:32,500 --> 00:15:33,580
and nothing would happen.

251
00:15:34,360 --> 00:15:35,240
But look at you,

252
00:15:35,620 --> 00:15:37,030
acting like a lovesick fool.

253
00:15:37,670 --> 00:15:39,120
If something really happened to you,

254
00:15:39,120 --> 00:15:40,670
how would I explain it to our parents?

255
00:15:44,670 --> 00:15:45,940
Don't go out anymore.

256
00:15:46,620 --> 00:15:48,200
Driving for the lady boss during the day,

257
00:15:48,440 --> 00:15:49,860
and warming the bed
for a sick woman at night.

258
00:15:49,860 --> 00:15:51,010
You'll get into trouble sooner or later.

259
00:15:51,170 --> 00:15:52,750
How... How can you talk like that?

260
00:15:52,750 --> 00:15:54,530
Do you think that sounds nice?

261
00:15:54,530 --> 00:15:55,760
What do you mean?

262
00:15:55,790 --> 00:15:56,620
Let me ask you,

263
00:15:56,620 --> 00:15:57,620
do you have anything else
you're hiding from me?

264
00:15:59,940 --> 00:16:01,120
If you hide anything else from me,

265
00:16:01,120 --> 00:16:02,150
I won't let you off easy.

266
00:16:02,150 --> 00:16:03,290
Don't you wave your hands at me.

267
00:16:43,480 --> 00:16:44,150
Ma'am,

268
00:16:44,670 --> 00:16:45,960
I want to ask you about someone.

269
00:16:46,600 --> 00:16:48,000
Does Hao Jie live here?

270
00:16:59,480 --> 00:17:00,150
Hello.

271
00:17:09,160 --> 00:17:10,310
What do you want from me?

272
00:17:11,609 --> 00:17:13,220
I didn't break you two up.

273
00:17:13,220 --> 00:17:14,700
We grew up together.

274
00:17:14,700 --> 00:17:16,660
First come, first served.
I was there first.

275
00:17:16,660 --> 00:17:18,000
I didn't do anything wrong to you.

276
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:18,920
He promised me.

277
00:17:18,920 --> 00:17:20,220
He's the one who wronged me.

278
00:17:20,220 --> 00:17:20,720
No—

279
00:17:21,030 --> 00:17:21,440
Ma'am.

280
00:17:21,440 --> 00:17:21,960
Ma'am.

281
00:17:21,960 --> 00:17:23,420
Did you mistake me for someone else?

282
00:17:23,420 --> 00:17:24,720
What are you talking about?

283
00:17:25,240 --> 00:17:27,250
My name is Liu Juan.

284
00:17:27,250 --> 00:17:28,250
I'm a cop from

285
00:17:28,250 --> 00:17:29,500
Yuhong Square Police Station.

286
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:31,810
I came to ask Hao Jie a few things.

287
00:17:31,810 --> 00:17:33,050
That's all.

288
00:17:33,050 --> 00:17:34,060
Look at you—

289
00:17:34,240 --> 00:17:35,420
What are you even saying?

290
00:17:36,250 --> 00:17:37,860
You're a cop?

291
00:17:37,920 --> 00:17:39,240
Don't get worked up.

292
00:17:39,240 --> 00:17:40,310
Then d-did you

293
00:17:40,310 --> 00:17:41,570
find my money?

294
00:17:42,420 --> 00:17:43,290
W-What money?

295
00:17:43,290 --> 00:17:44,380
-My money's gone.
-When did you lose it?

296
00:17:44,380 --> 00:17:45,310
When did you lose the money?

297
00:17:45,330 --> 00:17:45,990
Where'd you lose it?

298
00:17:46,050 --> 00:17:46,500
No, my money—

299
00:17:46,500 --> 00:17:47,140
Don't panic. Wait—

300
00:17:47,140 --> 00:17:48,330
-Don't go.
-I need to go find the police!

301
00:17:48,460 --> 00:17:50,240
-My money's gone.
-Calm down. Calm down.

302
00:17:50,240 --> 00:17:51,270
Ma'am, listen to me.

303
00:17:51,420 --> 00:17:52,440
Found it. I found it.

304
00:17:52,610 --> 00:17:53,570
I found it. Look, let me—

305
00:17:53,570 --> 00:17:54,310
Sit down first. Let me...

306
00:17:54,310 --> 00:17:55,030
tell you.

307
00:17:55,030 --> 00:17:55,880
Look where it is.

308
00:17:55,880 --> 00:17:56,680
Then where is my money?

309
00:17:56,680 --> 00:17:57,510
L-Look,

310
00:17:57,510 --> 00:17:58,240
is this it?

311
00:17:59,010 --> 00:17:59,810
Yes.

312
00:18:00,740 --> 00:18:02,150
Well, thank you.

313
00:18:02,220 --> 00:18:03,550
You're welcome. Well...

314
00:18:03,550 --> 00:18:04,380
Well...

315
00:18:04,770 --> 00:18:05,810
-Is this the right amount?
-Yes, yes.

316
00:18:05,810 --> 00:18:06,350
Isn't it too much?

317
00:18:06,350 --> 00:18:08,050
Don't touch it. This is my money.

318
00:18:08,050 --> 00:18:09,380
Don't touch my money.

319
00:18:10,740 --> 00:18:11,750
What a mess.

320
00:18:11,750 --> 00:18:13,310
Didn't get anything done, and lost fifty.

321
00:18:13,850 --> 00:18:15,560
I must owe this family.

322
00:18:15,940 --> 00:18:17,440
What a killer of a day.

323
00:18:18,770 --> 00:18:19,500
Found it.

324
00:18:19,940 --> 00:18:20,770
Found the money.
